---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { GITHUB_REPO_URL, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

const description =
	"About this sample: a custom blog built and deployed end to end.";
---

<Layout title={`About - ${SITE_TITLE}`} description={description}>
	<h1>About</h1>
	<p>
		I'm building gcp-demos: a handful of small apps, each one a real,
		end-to-end demo of a particular stack, deployed the way a real product
		would be - real infra, real third-party services in test/sandbox mode
		where money's involved, real bugs. This blog is one of them.
	</p>
	<p>
		This is an Astro site. It serves prerendered HTML for static pages and
		renders other pages on the fly by fetching content from a self-hosted
		Payload CMS instance running alongside it.
	</p>
	<h2>Not a real publication</h2>
	<p>
		If you're looking at this expecting a real publication - it isn't one -
		it merely exists to showcase the integration of Astro with Payload, and
		the real Docker releases and GCP infrastructure behind both.&nbsp;
		<a href={GITHUB_REPO_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
			View on GitHub
		</a>
	</p>
</Layout>
